MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Best of Bread fits the mellow, nostalgic listening I associate with Simon & Garfunkel and my older-hit collections.",
    "The Beach Boys and Elvis collections offer familiar older songs, with The Beach Boys especially close to my interest in mid-’60s pop."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Adele’s albums and x feel less connected to the older pop and rock hits I want now; my interest in Born This Way does not mean every contemporary pop album appeals equally.",
    "Blake Shelton’s collection has the greatest-hits format I like, but country music is not what I am seeking today. To All The Girls... and Title give me too little recognizable musical context to choose confidently."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "A greatest-hits collection is appealing only when the artist and songs also fit; the format alone does not make Blake Shelton a close match.",
    "My occasional interest in contemporary pop seems to have been treated as a broader preference than it is right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The repeated connection among AM Gold, classic-rock hits, Simon & Garfunkel, and Melanie matters because I am looking for familiar older pop, folk, and rock songs.",
    "Cheek to Cheek makes a duet album like Partners potentially appealing if it is Barbra Streisand’s, but that is a secondary interest behind the classic-hit collections today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my taste for familiar collections, but stretched that preference too far beyond the older pop and rock I currently want."
}
